{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather to Me, etc., from the elders of Israel.</b> And He did not say ״Gather to Me, etc., seventy elders of Israel״ — this alludes to what they said of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 15:21), that the seventy elders whom he gathered in Egypt were all killed together with Hur. Therefore He said to him that he should gather seventy others from the elders of Israel. And He said the word <b>to Me</b> — that he should intend in this matter for the sake of His name, blessed be He, so that the Satan not mislead him with an elder who is not fit; and when it is for the sake of His name, blessed be He, ״a keeper of a commandment knows no evil thing״ (Ecclesiastes 8:5)." "<b>Further,</b> it is intended that their gathering be to HaShem — that they should receive the appointment and authority from HaShem over Israel and not from Moses. Further, it intends to say to them: even though the first elders were killed, they should not hold themselves back from approaching the appointment; even though they may be gathered — meaning, killed — to Me, for My name's sake, in the manner of what it says (Psalms 44:23) ״כִּי עָלֶיךָ הוֹרַגְנוּ״." "<b>Elders of the people and its officers.</b> Meaning, they are esteemed in the eyes of the people and able to rule over them and they will tremble at their word — and this is the meaning of <b>and its officers.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:37.801045834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}